{%- comment -%}
  Snippet: product-accordion
  Phase 4, Stage 6. One expand/collapse panel built on native <details>/
  <summary> — the browser provides the disclosure semantics (keyboard
  operability, and an implicit expanded/collapsed state exposed to
  assistive tech) with zero JavaScript, so this works identically with JS
  fully disabled. The chevron's open/closed rotation is pure CSS, keyed off
  the browser-managed details[open] attribute (theme.css section 39) — no
  aria-expanded/toggle-event listener is added, since native <summary>
  already communicates the same state correctly on its own, and a manually
  synced ARIA attribute would only add a way for the two to drift out of
  sync for no accessibility benefit.

  Params:
    heading - required, plain text shown in the summary row
    content - required, HTML string shown in the expanded panel
              (product.description or a richtext setting's rendered output)
    id      - required, unique value for this instance (block.id) used to
              give the <details> element a stable, unique id
    block   - optional, a section block object; when given,
              block.shopify_attributes is applied so the block behaves
              correctly in the Theme Editor (select/highlight/reorder)
{%- endcomment -%}
<details class="product-accordion__item" id="ProductAccordion-{{ id }}" data-product-accordion {% if block %}{{ block.shopify_attributes }}{% endif %}>
  <summary class="product-accordion__summary">
    <span class="product-accordion__heading">{{ heading }}</span>
    <span class="product-accordion__icon" aria-hidden="true">
      {%- render 'icon', icon: 'chevron-down', size: 18 -%}
    </span>
  </summary>
  <div class="product-accordion__panel">
    <div class="product-accordion__content rte">
      {{ content }}
    </div>
  </div>
</details>
